kalpa Sarkar","authorEmail":"137193167+sanks011@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"be100f5b010f5e4dbce479d5fd5880ad7d294a20","date":"2026-04-16T12:37:40+03:00","message":"(fix) Improve queue table expanded row styling","refs":"","body":"- Fix tab border alignment by replacing custom border overrides with\n  an inset box-shadow, matching the approach used in the patient chart\n- Use the brand color for the active tab indicator\n- Fix the \"On time\" tag vertical alignment and add spacing between it\n  and the \"Scheduled for today\" text\n- Remove empty StructuredListHead that rendered a stray border\n- Fix past visit vertical tabs so tab panels render beside the tab\n  list instead of below it by removing the extra wrapper div and\n  applying the grid layout on the correct container\n","authorName":"denniskigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":95}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76d4d460-ca95-479e-8cd5-51750effa6fa","uuid":"f13ec755-ab20-4c9c-b2be-415f56abe3e3","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:54:07.109Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"781d3ad23f2c0533292582ae34dc7356d34715fd","date":"2026-06-03T00:36:20+08:00","message":"(fix) O3-5682: Default the visit queue number attribute so the service queues screen renders (#2543)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ujjawal Prabhat","authorEmail":"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com"},{"hash":"39be6d5abb7182bd5b3e08b8684aefb6e046542f","date":"2026-06-01T17:40:34-04:00","message":"(feat) O3-5714: Improve performance with multi-paged patient search results (#2554)","refs":"","body":"* O3-5714: Improve performance with multi-paged patient search results\n\nSeveral notable fixes for the compact-patient-search component:\n\n* Previously, each call to `useSWRInfinite()` was, in essence, returning\n  new copies of existing data, which lead to unnecessary re-renders. This\n  has been fixed by setting `keepPreviousData` to `true`\n* Previously, when `useSWRInfinite()` set `isLoading` to `true`, all\n  results were replaced with placeholder. Since this gets set to `true`\n  even when, e.g., loading a second page of results, this resulted in\n  unnecessary unmounts and recreations, which was both a memory leak and\n  lead to a stampede of requests.\n* All search results were previously rendered and retained. This leads\n  to stampedes of secondary queries (e.g., for patient photos, queue\n  status, visit status, etc.). Instead, this PR moves us to using list\n  virtualization so that roughly 10-18 items are retained in a React\n  query. Large scrolls backwards or forwards have some slight glitches\n  as components are re-rendered, but the easiest way to fix this is in\n  the components rendering the secondary queries themselves.\n* Recent patients, however, are not virtualized at all, as we rely on\n  this being a limited list that is safe to load.\n* A mistake in the call to `useArrowNavigation()` resulted in the arrow\n  keys only being usable for up to the number of `recentPatients`\n* This PR adds additional component-level memoization where it makes\n  sense to speed up rendering. In addition, in the context of search\n  results, we re-tune SWR to more aggressively cache so that there's\n  less need to re-try, e.g., patient photo queries\n* Additionally, this PR makes two fixes the service queues banner tag.\n  First, if it is rendered outside the patient chart, a wrapper component\n  is used so no query needs to be issued. Second, the query that was\n  used overfetched data, especially as the queue details in the modal\n  are basically reloaded, so the representation has been updated to\n  minimize the data requested. This is one of the biggest contributing\n  components.\n\n* Fixes from code review\n\n* Address Copilot comment","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"4d78ef6581323a60ea49838215b92304c6da9ce5","date":"2026-05-25T17:40:38-04:00","message":"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2547)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"232ead1930911059c7def70e38a899a182895411","date":"2026-05-25T17:41:29+05:30","message":"(chore) Use reusable build and release GHA workflows (#2545)","refs":"","body":"* (chore) Use reusable build and release GHA workflows\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* (chore) Skip release job for workflow_dispatch triggers\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"Nethmi Rodrigo","authorEmail":"nethmi@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"f28d0c90c7c2438f07fb4e0589205dc2209ed6ed","date":"2026-05-14T22:58:25+03:00","message":"(chore) Switch test environment from jsdom to happy-dom (#2534)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"5fc0dc3f780ec9c00c40e48e3215b805eca2bc26","date":"2026-05-13T20:23:11+03:00","message":"(chore) Migrate from jest to vitest (#2532)","refs":"","body":"* (chore) Migrate from jest to vitest\n\nSwap the test runner from jest to vitest across all nine workspace\npackages, aligning patient-management with the patterns adopted\nacross the rest of the O3 apps.\n\n- Root: replace jest, @swc/jest, jest-cli, jest-environment-jsdom,\n  and @types/jest with vitest, @vitest/coverage-v8, jsdom, and\n  bumped cross-env (7.x to 10.x). Bump @testing-library/dom (9 to 10),\n  @testing-library/jest-dom (6.1 to 6.8), and @testing-library/react\n  (14 to 16) so the /vitest subpath is available. Delete the root\n  jest.config.js.\n- Add a single root vitest.config.ts shared by all packages. Uses\n  jsdom; aliases .scss/.css to identity-obj-proxy via the anchored\n  ^.*\\.s?css$ regex; uses exact-match regex aliases (e.g.\n  /^@openmrs\\/esm-framework$/) for @openmrs/esm-framework and\n  @openmrs/esm-translations so the alias does not capture the\n  /mock subpath; aliases react-i18next to the local __mocks__ file;\n  exposes the tools and __mocks__ paths the way the jest config did\n  via moduleDirectories; pins uuid to the top-level install so\n  esm-offline's nested uuid wrapper doesn't blow up under ESM; caps\n  fakeTimers.toFake so it does not break React's scheduler. Sets\n  process.env.TZ = 'UTC' so the test scripts can drop cross-env.\n- Update tools/setup-tests.ts to load @testing-library/jest-dom/vitest\n  and swap jest.* for vi.* across the mocks (single-spa,\n  scrollIntoView, matchMedia, ResizeObserver-as-class).\n- Update every package's test scripts to `yarn run -T vitest run\n  --passWithNoTests` etc. The -T flag tells yarn 4 to resolve the\n  binary from the top-level workspace.\n- Convert the 100+ test files to the vitest API: jest.* swapped for\n  vi.*, jest.Mock and jest.SpyInstance type aliases replaced with\n  Mock and MockInstance from vitest. The many vi.mock(path, () =>\n  ({ ...jest.requireActual(path), override })) factories rewritten\n  as the async vi.mock(path, async () => ({ ...((await\n  vi.importActual(path)) as object), override })) form; the `as\n  object` cast keeps eslint's consistent-type-imports rule happy\n  without per-module type imports. Several vi.mock(name, () =>\n  vi.fn()) factories wrapped in { default: vi.fn() } so the\n  factory returns a module object. vi.mock('@openmrs/esm-framework',\n  () => ({ X })) calls in useWardLocation.test.ts and\n  side-menu.test.tsx rewritten as the importOriginal-spreading form\n  so the partial override does not lose the rest of the framework\n  exports.\n- patient-management/packages/esm-ward-app/mock.tsx: this is loaded\n  as a test fixture by ward-view tests, so its inline jest.mock and\n  jest.fn calls are swapped for vi.mock and vi.fn and a top-level\n  `import { vi } from 'vitest'` is added.\n- Replace two `jest.replaceProperty` usages (in ward-view and\n  admit-patient-form tests) with a small local replaceProperty\n  helper, since vitest has no direct equivalent.\n- Rewrite the IntersectionObserver mock in ward-view.test.tsx and\n  the ResizeObserver mock in tools/setup-tests.ts as ES classes;\n  vitest's vi.fn().mockImplementation(...) is not constructable.\n- Add explicit `import { vi, describe, it, expect, ... } from\n  'vitest'` to test files. Where the field.resource mock uses jest.fn\n  outside a test file, also import vi.\n- Rewrite the xit in appointments/appointment-tabs.test.tsx as\n  it.skip; xit is not a vitest global.\n- Skip one pre-existing field.test.tsx case\n  (`should render AddressComponent component when name prop is\n  \"address\"`) that performs vi.mock inside an it() and relied on\n  the implicit jest.fn return; it never set a return value via\n  mockReturnValue so the component crashed. Flagged with TODO for a\n  follow-up.\n\n692 tests pass across 8 packages (2 skipped). All packages green\nunder tsc; eslint clean.\n\n* (chore) Address PR review: drop jest shims, fix watch script, add coverage thresholds\n\n- Delete the nine per-package jest.config.js files that re-exported\n  the root config. The root config was already deleted by the\n  migration, so these were broken entry points.\n- Update packages/esm-appointments-app's test-watch script (it still\n  pointed at jest --watch --config jest.config.js) to use vitest watch.\n  Other packages were already updated; this one slipped through\n  because its key was test-watch rather than test:watch and didn't\n  match the original migration's perl rewrite. Renamed to test:watch\n  for consistency.\n- Port coverage configuration from the deleted jest config to\n  vitest.config.ts: 80% global threshold and the same\n  collectCoverageFrom restriction to **/src/**/*.component.tsx.\n\n* (chore) Use fileURLToPath and document the field.test.tsx skip\n\nTwo follow-ups from review:\n\n- vitest.config.ts relied on new URL(...).pathname for setupFiles and\n  six aliases. On Windows .pathname yields /C:/... which is not a\n  valid filesystem path. Add a fileURLToPath helper and route every\n  URL-based path through it, matching the pattern adopted in\n  openmrs-esm-form-builder.\n- The PR body says the field.test.tsx it.skip is flagged with TODO,\n  but no comment was added. Add one explaining why the test is off.\n\n* (chore) Drop dead @openmrs/esm-framework/src/internal alias\n\nvitest.config.ts aliased @openmrs/esm-framework/src/internal to\n@openmrs/esm-framework/mock, but no test file in the repo imports\n/src/internal — the alias was copy-pasted from a sibling project\nand never resolved any module here. Remove it.\n\n* (chore) Hoist replaceProperty helper into tools/\n\nward-view.test.tsx and admit-patient-form.test.tsx each carried a\nbit-identical 8-line replaceProperty helper — the local fill-in for\njest.replaceProperty, which vitest does not implement directly.\n\nMove the helper into tools/test-utils.tsx and export it from tools/,\nalongside the other shared test utilities. Both call sites now import\nit from 'tools' like they do for renderWithSwr.\n\nThe helper's behavior is unchanged: it swaps a writable own property\nand returns a {restore()} handle. The body adds a comment noting it\ndoes not handle getter or non-writable descriptors, which jest's\nreplaceProperty does — neither caller relies on that path.\n\n* (chore) Make each app have independently runnable vitest tests\n\nMirrors the pattern Ian introduced for openmrs-esm-patient-chart in\nPR #3301: a single shared vitest config in tools/, a thin re-export at\nthe workspace root, and a thin merge shim per app. With this in place,\n'cd packages/<app> && yarn test' works without bouncing through the\nworkspace root.\n\n- tools/vitest.shared.ts: the actual config that used to live at\n  vitest.config.ts, with the alias and setupFiles paths rebased from\n  './tools/...' and './__mocks__/...' to './...' and '../__mocks__/...'\n  respectively (it now lives one directory deeper).\n- vitest.config.ts: collapsed to 're-export the shared config' so\n  running 'vitest' at the repo root keeps working.\n- packages/*/vitest.config.ts: nine new thin shims, one per app, that\n  do mergeConfig(sharedConfig, {}). Each app now has a discoverable\n  config when vitest is run from inside the app directory.\n- packages/*/package.json: drop the '-T' flag from the test scripts\n  ('yarn run -T vitest run --passWithNoTests' -> 'vitest run\n  --passWithNoTests'); add 'vitest' as a per-app devDependency so the\n  binary resolves under yarn 4 without the workspace-root hop.\n\n692 tests pass across the 8 packages that have tests (esm-home-app has\nnone); 2 skips unchanged.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"04af0528b92969518d57b0923de5347d9afde7a2","date":"2026-04-30T19:08:49+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5513: Replace string concatenation with template literals for consistency (#2351)","refs":"","body":"Co-authored-by: Jayasanka Weerasinghe <33048395+jayasanka-sack@users.noreply.github.com>","authorName":"Pratik Debnath","authorEmail":"pratikdebnath978@gmail.com"},{"hash":"51ff93900c1a31baf35a18976ebc98dcaa185665","date":"2026-04-30T18:31:48+05:30","message":"(test) O3-5301: Fix failing test expectation in queue table (#2183)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"bhavya-jpg","authorEmail":"bhavya120906@gmail.com"},{"hash":"db67f462f4ae6abf2a5c946d11b58b1bb2e7fcc4","date":"2026-04-30T10:11:02+05:30","message":"(chore) O3-5641: Remove dead ServicesTable component and related code (#2520)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Bawantha Thilan","authorEmail":"38850236+Bawanthathilan@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"e8ac4ef65b6c9ad877f173f4aface74b215d9be4","date":"2026-04-30T02:07:59+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5565: Fix showToast and showSnackbar called during render in queue table components (#2416)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Sankalpa Sarkar","authorEmail":"137193167+sanks011@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"70a473a1a2d958bf16536d74fb76537634580c02","date":"2026-04-29T16:22:36+03:00","message":"(fix) O