{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CSXUg8VZwdjqgMmUZcqyHY","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"a7bd67168e3db4b095f8a1c06451549d3ec77b79","date":"2026-10-14T19:25:14+05:30","message":"(feat) O3-6098: Show today's appointments and visit attribute tags in the current visit summary (#2824)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Nethmi Rodrigo","authorEmail":"nethmi@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"b8335ad593a4946dd297a88e00c1fd6e6d1fc4f0","date":"2026-09-08T20:40:11+08:00","message":"(fix) O3-5940: Don't offer queues a patient is already in (#2710)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) O3-5940: Don't offer queues a patient is already in\n\n* (fix) O3-5940: Don't submit a prefilled service before the entries load\n\nA service prefilled from the dashboard was submittable while the lookup of the\npatient's queue entries was still in flight: the queues had loaded, so the\npriority defaulted and the form was valid behind the Service skeleton, and a\nquick submit posted a queue entry that the filter would have excluded a moment\nlater. The priority default now waits for those entries, so submitting during\nthat window fails validation instead of reaching the server.\n\n* (fix) O3-5940: Let the Service field carry the queue filtering on its own\n\nFiltering whole locations out of the Location dropdown required a second,\nunscoped useQueues() call just to group queues by location, plus a reset\neffect to clear a location that disappeared underneath the user. Drop both\nand filter only the Service options, which already load scoped to the\nselected location. When the patient is in every queue there, the select\nrenders empty with helper text saying so, and the required error is\nsuppressed so it does not replace that text on blur. The misconfiguration\nnotice now keys off the unfiltered queue list, and the priority skeleton\nwaits on the queue entries alongside the services.\n\nDuplicate submissions come back as a generic \"Invalid Submission\" message\nwith the identifying code in globalErrors, so getErrorMessage appends those\ncodes and the queue fields reuse isDuplicateQueueEntryError instead of\nmatching the message alone.\n\n* (fix) O3-5940: Address review feedback on duplicate detection and the Service field\n\nRead the duplicate error code from `globalErrors`, where the backend actually\nreports it, and keep `getErrorMessage` free of it so the code no longer leaks\ninto the snackbar subtitle two modals build from it. Let a genuine validation\nerror still surface on the Service field, with the \"already in every queue\"\nmessage carried as its error text rather than suppressing `invalid`.\n\nAlso make `patientUuid` optional, since every caller passes a value that may be\nundefined, and drop the `memoizedQueueLocations` memo: `useFhirFetchAll` returns\na fresh array on every render, so its dependency never matched and the memo\nnever once returned a cached value.\n\n* Fix duplicate-queue error messages and prefilled service edge case\n\n- Read globalErrors from the backend response so validation errors like\n  \"already in this queue\" surface instead of a generic message.\n- Clear a prefilled service selection once queue entries confirm the\n  patient is already enrolled in it.\n\n* (fix) O3-5940: Warn when the active queue entry lookup fails\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\nCo-authored-by: NethmiRodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>","authorName":"Ujjawal Prabhat","authorEmail":"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com"},{"hash":"7212897e35ee9efa79192770f019651dcbd66cc1","date":"2026-08-28T18:42:34+08:00","message":"(feat) O3-5763: Unify the Current visit and Previous visit views (#2600)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) O3-5763: Unify the Current visit and Previous visit views\n\n* (fix) O3-5763: Address review feedback on unified visit summary\n\n* (fix) Restore visit note authoring on the Current visit tab\n\n* (fix) O3-5763: Fix obs group crash, encounter editing and expanded row styles\n\n* (fix) O3-5763: Fix the e2e specs covering the unified visit summary\n\nServe the patient notes app in the e2e frontend, scope the encounter assertions\nto the expanded row's table, and revalidate queue entries once per submit rather\nthan twice.\n\n* (fix) O3-5763: Analyze the e2e database before running the specs\n\nThe seeded image reports zero rows for every table, so MariaDB plans the queue\nentry query, whose join spans ~44 tables, from full scans. That is harmless while\nqueue_entry is empty and takes minutes once a spec inserts a row, hanging\nservice-queues.spec.ts. Analyzing the schema takes under a second.\n\nAlso adds the mutate mock that usePastVisits now returns to the PastVisit tests.\n\n* (fix) O3-5763: Address review feedback on the unified visit summary\n\nMoves the queue spec's API setup into e2e/commands so other queue specs can reuse\nit, guards its teardown against a partial setup, and scopes the encounter locator\nto the table. Also guards the edit handler against an unresolved patient, restores\nthe date validity check, widens the form entry window to match the chart, and\ncovers the past visit filter and the slot state in tests.\n\n* (fix) O3-5763: Hand the visit summary our mutate for encounter deletes\n\nDeleting an encounter opens a modal rather than a workspace, so the workspace\nsubscription never fires and both tabs kept showing the deleted encounter.\nPairs with the chart accepting mutateVisitContext alongside onEditEncounter.\n\n* (fix) O3-5763: Wait for the patient before mounting the vitals extension\n\nThe vitals extension reads  during render — with a nonzero\nbmiMinimumAge, shouldShowBmi reaches patient.birthDate before the extension's\nown loading guard — so mounting it while usePatient is still resolving throws\ninto the error boundary. Extends the existing patient-loading test to cover it.\n\n* (chore) O3-5763: Drop the CI database statistics workaround\n\nThe queue entry list was slow because the module fetched its associations\neagerly, not because of the image. Fixed properly in openmrs-module-queue#122,\nso this step comes out.\n\n* (feat) O3-5763: Hand the patient down to the visit summary extension\n\nThe shared visit summary reads the patient from the chart store, which Service\nQueues never populates, so its embedded form view had nothing to render with.\nBoth tabs now pass `patient` in the slot state, and the slot assertions cover\n`patient`, `onEditEncounter` and `mutateVisitContext` so dropping one is caught\nhere rather than in the e2e run.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: jwnasambu <33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Ujjawal Prabhat <ujjawal@Ujjawals-MacBook-Pro.local>\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>","authorName":"Ujjawal Prabhat","authorEmail":"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com"},{"hash":"7251e36ba65dc9f0154009b89eb0a84db37ac85a","date":"2026-06-10T15:39:03+08:00","message":"(fix) O3-5665: Fix vitals form and triage form not opening (#2540)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) launch vitals and triage forms inline in service queues\n\n* translation changes\n\n* fixup\n\n* fixup: drop redundant visitContext from notes workspace launch\n\n* (fix) Address feedback\n\nMatch obs by concept UUID, isolate patient group props in a dedicated workspace group, rename triage-note to visit-note, and single-source workspace names.\n\n* (fix) Match obs by concept UUID behind a configurable visitNoteEncounterTypeUuid guard.\n\n* chore: update translations\n\n* chore: update translations\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: jwnasambu <33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\nCo-authored-by: NethmiRodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>","authorName":"Ujjawal Prabhat","authorEmail":"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":4}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76d4d460-ca95-479e-8cd5-51750effa6fa","uuid":"580558a1-c064-4179-af20-63fe742aef0d","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:54:15.611Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"a7bd67168e3db4b095f8a1c06451549d3ec77b79","date":"2026-10-14T19:25:14+05:30","message":"(feat) O3-6098: Show today's appointments and visit attribute tags in the current visit summary (#2824)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Nethmi Rodrigo","authorEmail":"nethmi@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"b8335ad593a4946dd297a88e00c1fd6e6d1fc4f0","date":"2026-09-08T20:40:11+08:00","message":"(fix) O3-5940: Don't offer queues a patient is already in (#2710)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) O3-5940: Don't offer queues a patient is already in\n\n* (fix) O3-5940: Don't submit a prefilled service before the entries load\n\nA service prefilled from the dashboard was submittable while the lookup of the\npatient's queue entries was still in flight: the queues had loaded, so the\npriority defaulted and the form was valid behind the Service skeleton, and a\nquick submit posted a queue entry that the filter would have excluded a moment\nlater. The priority default now waits for those entries, so submitting during\nthat window fails validation instead of reaching the server.\n\n* (fix) O3-5940: Let the Service field carry the queue filtering on its own\n\nFiltering whole locations out of the Location dropdown required a second,\nunscoped useQueues() call just to group queues by location, plus a reset\neffect to clear a location that disappeared underneath the user. Drop both\nand filter only the Service options, which already load scoped to the\nselected location. When the patient is in every queue there, the select\nrenders empty with helper text saying so, and the required error is\nsuppressed so it does not replace that text on blur. The misconfiguration\nnotice now keys off the unfiltered queue list, and the priority skeleton\nwaits on the queue entries alongside the services.\n\nDuplicate submissions come back as a generic \"Invalid Submission\" message\nwith the identifying code in globalErrors, so getErrorMessage appends those\ncodes and the queue fields reuse isDuplicateQueueEntryError instead of\nmatching the message alone.\n\n* (fix) O3-5940: Address review feedback on duplicate detection and the Service field\n\nRead the duplicate error code from `globalErrors`, where the backend actually\nreports it, and keep `getErrorMessage` free of it so the code no longer leaks\ninto the snackbar subtitle two modals build from it. Let a genuine validation\nerror still surface on the Service field, with the \"already in every queue\"\nmessage carried as its error text rather than suppressing `invalid`.\n\nAlso make `patientUuid` optional, since every caller passes a value that may be\nundefined, and drop the `memoizedQueueLocations` memo: `useFhirFetchAll` returns\na fresh array on every render, so its dependency never matched and the memo\nnever once returned a cached value.\n\n* Fix duplicate-queue error messages and prefilled service edge case\n\n- Read globalErrors from the backend response so validation errors like\n  \"already in this queue\" surface instead of a generic message.\n- Clear a prefilled service selection once queue entries confirm the\n  patient is already enrolled in it.\n\n* (fix) O3-5940: Warn when the active queue entry lookup fails\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\nCo-authored-by: NethmiRodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>","authorName":"Ujjawal Prabhat","authorEmail":"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com"},{"hash":"7212897e35ee9efa79192770f019651dcbd66cc1","date":"2026-08-28T18:42:34+08:00","message":"(feat) O3-5763: Unify the Current visit and Previous visit views (#2600)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) O3-5763: Unify the Current visit and Previous visit views\n\n* (fix) O3-5763: Address review feedback on unified visit summary\n\n* (fix) Restore visit note authoring on the Current visit tab\n\n* (fix) O3-5763: Fix obs group crash, encounter editing and expanded row styles\n\n* (fix) O3-5763: Fix the e2e specs covering the unified visit summary\n\nServe the patient notes app in the e2e frontend, scope the encounter assertions\nto the expanded row's table, and revalidate queue entries once per submit rather\nthan twice.\n\n* (fix) O3-5763: Analyze the e2e database before running the specs\n\nThe seeded image reports zero rows for every table, so MariaDB plans the queue\nentry query, whose join spans ~44 tables, from full scans. That is harmless while\nqueue_entry is empty and takes minutes once a spec inserts a row, hanging\nservice-queues.spec.ts. Analyzing the schema takes under a second.\n\nAlso adds the mutate mock that usePastVisits now returns to the PastVisit tests.\n\n* (fix) O3-5763: Address review feedback on the unified visit summary\n\nMoves the queue spec's API setup into e2e/commands so other queue specs can reuse\nit, guards its teardown against a partial setup, and scopes the encounter locator\nto the table. Also guards the edit handler against an unresolved patient, restores\nthe date validity check, widens the form entry window to match the chart, and\ncovers the past visit filter and the slot state in tests.\n\n* (fix) O3-5763: Hand the visit summary our mutate for encounter deletes\n\nDeleting an encounter opens a modal rather than a workspace, so the workspace\nsubscription never fires and both tabs kept showing the deleted encounter.\nPairs with the chart accepting mutateVisitContext alongside onEditEncounter.\n\n* (fix) O3-5763: Wait for the patient before mounting the vitals extension\n\nThe vitals extension reads  during render — with a nonzero\nbmiMinimumAge, shouldShowBmi reaches patient.birthDate before the extension's\nown loading guard — so mounting it while usePatient is still resolving throws\ninto the error boundary. Extends the existing patient-loading test to cover it.\n\n* (chore) O3-5763: Drop the CI database statistics workaround\n\nThe queue entry list was slow because the module fetched its associations\neagerly, not because of the image. Fixed properly in openmrs-module-queue#122,\nso this step comes out.\n\n* (feat) O3-5763: Hand the patient down to the visit summary extension\n\nThe shared visit summary reads the patient from the chart store, which Service\nQueues never populates, so its embedded form view had nothing to render with.\nBoth tabs now pass `patient` in the slot state, and the slot assertions cover\n`patient`, `onEditEncounter` and `mutateVisitContext` so dropping one is caught\nhere rather than in the e2e run.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: jwnasambu <33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Ujjawal Prabhat <ujjawal@Ujjawals-MacBook-Pro.local>\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>","authorName":"Ujjawal Prabhat","authorEmail":"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com"},{"hash":"7251e36ba65dc9f0154009b89eb0a84db37ac85a","date":"2026-06-10T15:39:03+08:00","message":"(fix) O3-5665: Fix vitals form and triage form not opening (#2540)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) launch vitals and triage forms inline in service queues\n\n* translation changes\n\n* fixup\n\n* fixup: drop redundant visitContext from notes workspace launch\n\n* (fix) Address feedback\n\nMatch obs by concept UUID, isolate patient group props in a dedicated workspace group, rename triage-note to visit-note, and single-source workspace names.\n\n* (fix) Match obs by concept UUID behind a configurable visitNoteEncounterTypeUuid guard.\n\n* chore: update translations\n\n* chore: update translations\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: jwnasambu <33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\nCo-authored-by: NethmiRodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>","authorName":"Ujjawal Prabhat","authorEmail":"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":4}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CSXUg8VZwdjqgMmUZcqyHY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
